erve1=112540606575770623396180, uint32 _blockTimestampLast=1611515181) [0x795065dcc9f64b5614c407a6efdc400da6221fb0] (Gas: 1217, [S: 0/L: 1])  // getReserves() → reserve0(SUSHI)=18654959824231177621943891, reserve1(WETH)=112540606575770623396180\n├── [16319] [STATICCALL] SushiMaker.token0() -> (address =SushiToken) [0x795065dcc9f64b5614c407a6efdc400da6221fb0] (Gas: 1149, [S: 0/L: 1])  // pair.token0() → SUSHI. Since fromToken=WETH=token1, this is amount0Out swap.\n├── [16945] [CALL] SushiMaker.transfer(address dst=UniswapV2Pair, uint256 wad=65658225521930163415) -> (bool =True) [0xc02aaa39b223fe8d0a0e5c4f27ead9083c756cc2] (Gas: 10962)  // Transfer 65.658 WETH (combined: 65.657 + 0.001) from SushiMaker to SUSHI/WETH pool\n└── [19191] [CALL] SushiMaker.swap(uint256 amount0Out=10844682068505278758672, uint256 amount1Out=0, address to=0x8798249c2e607446efb7ad49ec89dd1865ff4272, bytes data=0x) -> () [0x795065dcc9f64b5614c407a6efdc400da6221fb0] (Gas: 56433, Logs: 1, [S: 2/L: 3])  // [FINAL SWAP] swap(amount0Out=10844682068505278758672, amount1Out=0, to=SushiBar). Swaps 65.658 WETH → 10844.682 SUSHI. Sent to SushiBar (0x8798249c...).\n    ├── [17935] [CALL] UniswapV2Pair.transfer(address recipient=0x8798249c2e607446efb7ad49ec89dd1865ff4272, uint256 amount=10844682068505278758672) -> (bool =True) [0x6b3595068778dd592e39a122f4f5a5cf09c90fe2] (Gas: 14525)  // Transfer 10844.682 SUSHI to SushiBar (xSUSHI staking contract).\n    ├── [18196] [STATICCALL] UniswapV2Pair.balanceOf(address account=UniswapV2Pair) -> (uint256 =18644115142162672343185219) [0x6b3595068778dd592e39a122f4f5a5cf09c90fe2] (Gas: 1278, [S: 0/L: 1])\n    └── [18383] [STATICCALL] UniswapV2Pair.balanceOf(address =UniswapV2Pair) -> (uint256 =112606264801292553559595) [0xc02aaa39b223fe8d0a0e5c4f27ead9083c756cc2] (Gas: 1234, [S: 0/L: 1])", 'fix_report': '{\n    "vulnerability_type": "Business Logic Flaw — Missing Liquidity Validation + Unvalidated Default Bridge",\n    "faulty_functions": [\n        {\n            "function_name": "bridgeFor(address)",\n            "trigger_point": {\n                "transaction_hash": "0x747088ed3054d66fbd2c2ec6f6e0b077e71c3155dab0d56ccea2b5841903738f",\n                "index": 8244\n            },\n            "fault_description": "When a token has no explicitly configured bridge in the _bridges mapping, bridgeFor() silently defaults to WETH. This allows the attacker to route any token through any WETH-paired pool, including ones they create with microscopic liquidity. For DIGG and WBTC, no bridges were set, so both defaulted to WETH.",\n            "fix_strategy": "Require that a bridge must be explicitly configured via setBridge() before a token can be converted. Revert if no bridge is set instead of defaulting to WETH silently.",\n            "core_patch_snippet": "// Original vulnerability:\\nfunction bridgeFor(address token) public view returns (address bridge) {\\n    bridge = _bridges[token];\\n    if (bridge == address(0)) {\\n        bridge = weth;   // ← DANGEROUS DEFAULT\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n// Repair:\\nfunction bridgeFor(address token) public view returns (address bridge) {\\n    bridge = _bridges[token];\\n+   require(bridge != address(0), \\"SushiMaker: No bridge configured for token\\");\\n-   if (bridge == address(0)) {\\n-       bridge = weth;\\n-   }\\n}"\n        },\n        {\n            "function_name": "_swap(address,address,uint256,address)",\n            "trigger_point": {\n                "transaction_hash": "0x747088ed3054d66fbd2c2ec6f6e0b077e71c3155dab0d56ccea2b5841903738f",\n                "index": 12015\n            },\n            "fault_description": "After calling factory.getPair(fromToken, toToken), _swap() performs no validation on the pool\'s liquidity depth. It directly reads reserves and executes the swap. This allowed the attacker\'s pool with only 0.001 WETH and 0.000017211 DIGG to be used for a 1.14 DIGG swap, resulting in 99.91% value loss via extreme slippage.",\n            "fix_strategy": "Add a minimum liquidity threshold check before executing the swap. The product of reserves (k = reserve0 * reserve1) provides a reasonable liquidity metric. Alternatively, add a whitelist of approved pools or a minimum reserve requirement.",\n            "core_patch_snippet": "// Original vulnerability:\\nfunction _swap(address fromToken, address toToken, uint256 amountIn, address to) internal returns (uint256 amountOut) {\\n    IUniswapV2Pair pair = IUniswapV2Pair(factory.getPair(fromToken, toToken));\\n    require(address(pair) != address(0), \\"SushiMaker: Cannot convert\\");\\n    (uint256 reserve0, uint256 reserve1,) = pair.getReserves();\\n    // ... swap logic ...\\n}\\n\\n// Repair — add minimum liquidity threshold:\\nfunction _swap(address fromToken, address toToken, uint256 amountIn, address to) internal returns (uint256 amountOut) {\\n    IUniswapV2Pair pair = IUniswapV2Pair(factory.getPair(fromToken, toToken));\\n    require(address(pair) != address(0), \\"SushiMaker: Cannot convert\\");\\n    (uint256 reserve0, uint256 reserve1,) = pair.getReserves();\\n+   // Require minimum liquidity to prevent manipulation of shallow pools\\n+   uint256 minLiquidity = 1e18; // Minimum 1 ETH worth of liquidity\\n+   require(reserve0 >= minLiquidity && reserve1 >= minLiquidity, \\"SushiMaker: Pool liquidity too low\\");\\n    // ... swap logic ...\\n}"\n        },\n        {\n            "function_name": "_convertStep(address,address,uint256,uint256)",\n            "trigger_point": {\n                "transaction_hash": "0x747088ed3054d66fbd2c2ec6f6e0b077e71c3155dab0d56ccea2b5841903738f",\n                "index": 71\n            },\n            "fault_description": "The _convertStep function uses bridgeFor() to resolve intermediate tokens and then calls _swap() without validating the quality of the resolved bridge path. In the \'else\' branch (when neither token is SUSHI/WETH), both bridge0 and bridge1 default to WETH, causing both tokens to be swapped through potentially manipulated WETH-paired pools.",\n            "fix_strategy": "With the bridgeFor() and _swap() fixes above, this function is automatically protected. The bridgeFor() fix ensures only explicitly configured bridges are used, and the _swap() fix ensures only sufficiently liquid pools are used.",\n            "core_patch_snippet": "// This function is secured by fixing bridgeFor() and _swap() as described above.\\n// No additional changes needed for _convertStep() itself.\\n// The fixes to bridgeFor() will ensure only whitelisted bridges are used,\\n// and _swap() will reject pools with insufficient liquidity."\n        }\n    ]\n}'}</New_Insights>
