        "content": "SushiMaker Fee Conversion Exploit\n---\n\n1. Executive Summary\nOn February 1, 2021, an attacker exploited a **business logic flaw** in the **SushiMaker contract** (`0xe11fc0b43ab98eb91e9836129d1ee7c3bc95df50`), the official SushiSwap protocol fee converter. The attack resulted in the **theft of approximately 1.14 billion DIGG tokens** (≈$? at time of attack) by routing accumulated protocol fees through a self‑created microscopic‑liquidity pool.\nThe core vulnerability lies in the **combination of two insufficient validations**:\n- `bridgeFor()` defaults to WETH when no bridge is configured, allowing any token to be swapped through **any** WETH‑paired pool.\n- `_swap()` performs **no liquidity verification** on the pool returned by the factory, accepting even pools with reserves as low as 0.001 WETH.\nBy pre‑creating a DIGG/WETH pool with near‑zero liquidity and becoming its sole liquidity provider, the attacker forced the SushiMaker to execute a swap with extreme slippage, trapping the DIGG value in the attacker’s pool. The vulnerability has been **confirmed** through a successful patch verification, where the corrected contract reverted the attack transaction.\n---\n\n2.1 Core Vulnerability Mechanism\nThe SushiMaker contract is responsible for converting protocol fees (accumulated LP tokens) back into SUSHI and distributing them to the SushiBar. Two functions contain critical logic defects that allowed the attack:\n\n**Vulnerability 1: `bridgeFor()` – Unvalidated Default to WETH**\n```solidity\nfunction bridgeFor(address token) public view returns (address bridge) {\nbridge = _bridges[token];\nif (bridge == address(0)) {\nbridge = weth;   // ← DEFAULT FALLBACK WITH NO VALIDATION\n}\n}\n```\nIf a token (e.g., DIGG) was never explicitly configured via `setBridge()`, the function **silently returns WETH**. This means the converter will attempt to swap the token through **any** UniswapV2 pair between that token and WETH, regardless of its liquidity or legitimacy.\n\n**Vulnerability 2: `_swap()` – Missing Liquidity Validation**\n```solidity\nfunction _swap(address fromToken, address toToken, uint256 amountIn, address to) internal returns (uint256 amountOut) {\nIUniswapV2Pair pair = IUniswapV2...",
